# Live harness — the only proof that the MAS works

- `run_live_five.py` drives six real cases through Activity (`POST /cases` multipart, polls events, answers HITL like an engineer would — by option button, not by regex on the label): golden 1–2 (commissioning, group rebind), combat 0–3 (keep / keep-half / remove-half / new wells with a second workbook of parameters). Run via `python3 scripts/mas_gate.py --live [--cases id,id]` or directly with the Activity venv (`httpx`).
- A case **fails** when: status ≠ `done`; `.INC` mismatch; the same agent is re-delegated without new input (loop); `completion_review` escalation; `step_count > LIVE_STEP_BUDGET` (8); the same HITL question repeats after an answer; the orchestrator does not pick up a posted answer within `LIVE_HITL_RESUME_S` (180 s — `/answer` returns `waiting_user` immediately, resume is asynchronous); a gate asks to attach Excel while the case already has a workbook; `done` without `schedule_out`; machine text in any engineer-facing string. Do not relax these to make a run pass — fix the system.
- The six cases answer HITL with the option button (`choice`), so the orchestrator's `Interpret free-text answer` pass is **not** exercised by the gate. After touching the resume/interpret branch, also run one combat 3 case answering with prose only (expect `hitl.answered` with the interpreted `choice`) and one with an ambiguous answer (expect the clarify re-ask, then the button) — see Ревизия 7 in the plan for the reference cases.
- `.INC` comparison is **semantic** (`compare_schedules` in `golden-cases/run_ui_smoke.py`, reused by the harness): per DATES step, the set of keywords and the multiset of canonicalised records (`canon_record_tokens`: quotes, keyword case, `0.150`=`0.15`, trailing `1*`, record order inside a keyword). Whitespace, blank lines, comments, number formatting are not differences. A mismatch means a keyword missing/extra on a date or different parameter values — report those, never byte diffs.
- Goldens `golden-cases/*/…_MAS_result.INC` are reference answers: never overwrite without the user's explicit request. Combat fixtures are generated by `combat-dates-revise/run_cases_local.py` (`write_xlsx`, `new_well_params_rows`, `build_new_well_facts`) — change the generator, regenerate, keep xlsx and JSON facts identical.
- `PUBLISH_ACTIVITY=0 python3 combat-dates-revise/run_integration_cases.py` is the offline engine check (no n8n) — run after any commissioning/emit change.
- Live runs need the lab: `docker compose` services up, `python3 scripts/lab_soft_redeploy.py --skip-health` after template changes, `docker compose restart <svc>` after Python changes. Inspect a failing case with `python3 scripts/mas_trace_case.py CASE-… --n8n --node "<Node name>"`. Results: `_live_five_out/report.json`, `*_got.INC`.
- Add a case only when it proves a new behaviour (new HITL path, new artifact kind, new keyword family); keep the six-case gate under ~10 minutes.
